    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365-a1">

                <pb facs="0475" n="379" xml:id="pg379"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Powell to Mr. St.
                            Victor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1899-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1899</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 287.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Allow me to bring to your immediate notice
                    that at 10.30 this morning the premises of our legation were violated by one of
                    the general officers of the Government, in taking therefrom by force one who had
                    entered our legation.</p>
                <p>I consider this a gross violation of international courtesy that is due by you to
                    a Government that has ever been friendly and mindful of your national
                    interests.</p>
                <p>I am therefore compelled to ask that a suitable acknowledgment be made for this
                    invasion.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. F. Powell.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
